unreleased:

- added in-process suspension of running code (JS_RequestSuspend(),
  JS_IsSuspended(), JS_Resume())
- added heap snapshots (JS_WriteSnapshot(), JS_ReadSnapshot()): a
  runtime, including a suspended execution, can be saved and restored in
  another runtime or process
- added incremental snapshots (JS_SNAPSHOT_BASE, JS_SNAPSHOT_DELTA): a
  delta only contains the changes since a base snapshot; a modified
  object is saved as a patch of its base version
- a base snapshot is reproducible (the Math.random() state is saved in
  full snapshots and deltas, not in bases): a host can rebuild it
  instead of storing it
- added JS_SuspendCall() and JS_ResumeWith(): a C function suspends its
  JS caller until the host gives the result of the call
- added JS_IsSuspendException(), JS_IsUncatchableException(),
  JS_GetProgramBranchCount(), JS_IsEqual(), JS_NewProxy(), JS_IsProxy(),
  JS_GetProxyTarget(), JS_GetProxyHandler(), JS_GetTypedArrayType(),
  JS_GetFunctionProto() and JS_PromiseMarkAsHandled()
- added rquickjs/: the rquickjs Rust bindings built on this engine, with
  suspension, snapshots and the optional snapshot()/restore() builtins
- added TypeScript (JS_EVAL_FLAG_TYPESCRIPT; .ts/.mts/.cts files in qjs,
  qjsc and the module loader, qjs --typescript): types are erased while
  parsing; enums, namespaces and parameter properties are compiled to
  bytecode; const enum members are folded; imports only used as types
  are elided
- qjs --drepl file: durable REPL whose TypeScript commands run in a
  runtime saved to 'file' after each command (as a delta of a new
  session, rebuilt at startup) and restored from it at startup;
  qjs --typescript also applies to the REPL commands
- quickjs-libc: exported js_std_print() and js_std_console_log()
- quickjs-libc: js_module_normalize() resolves './x.js' / './x' to an
  existing './x.ts' ('./x.mjs' to './x.mts'); std.evalScript()
  'typescript' option; qjs: '-' as file name reads stdin
- fixed the export of the names bound by array destructuring exports
  ('export const [a, b] = ...', quickjs-ng #1576)
- added explicit resource management (ES2026): 'using' and 'await using'
  declarations, DisposableStack, AsyncDisposableStack, SuppressedError,
  Symbol.dispose, Symbol.asyncDispose, Iterator.prototype[Symbol.dispose]
  and %AsyncIteratorPrototype%[Symbol.asyncDispose], also in TypeScript;
  the dispose calls of 'using' declarations can be suspended and saved
  in snapshots, as can the stacks and a running disposeAsync()
- added standard decorators (2023-05) and auto-accessors ('accessor'),
  with Symbol.metadata
- added TypeScript legacy decorators (JS_EVAL_FLAG_TS_LEGACY_DECORATORS,
  qjs --experimental-decorators) and decorator metadata
  (JS_EVAL_FLAG_TS_DECORATOR_METADATA, qjs --emit-decorator-metadata),
  js_std_set_typescript_flags() and the std.evalScript() decorator options
- private getters and setters are named 'get #x' / 'set #x'
- bytecode version 7
- ported from quickjs-ng:
  - queueMicrotask(), atob()/btoa(), DOMException
    (JS_AddIntrinsicAToB(), JS_AddIntrinsicDOMException(),
    JS_ThrowDOMException())
  - Error.captureStackTrace(), Error.stackTraceLimit (default 10) and
    Error.prepareStackTrace() with CallSite objects; Error.prototype.stack
    is an accessor
  - promise hooks (JS_SetPromiseHook()) and faster %Promise% creation
  - C API: JS_NewObjectFrom(), JS_NewObjectFromStr(), JS_NewArrayFrom(),
    JS_GetLength(), JS_ToBigUint64(), JS_NewUint64(), JS_IsDate(),
    JS_IsRegExp(), JS_IsMap(), JS_IsSet(), JS_IsWeakRef(),
    JS_IsArrayBuffer(), JS_IsAsyncFunction(), JS_IsPromise(),
    JS_ThrowPlainError(), JS_NewSettledPromise(), JS_PromiseThen(),
    JS_GetPendingJobContext(), JS_FreeCStringRT(), JS_DupAtomRT(),
    JS_GetVersion(), QJS_VERSION_*, JS_GetInterruptHandler()
  - os.setInterval(), os.clearInterval(), os.exePath(), os.mkstemp(),
    os.mkdtemp(); 'text' and 'bytes' module types (import ... with
    { type: "text" }); js_module_test_json() replaced by
    js_module_get_type() and js_module_new_value()
  - fixes: Promise.withResolvers() double free on out of memory;
    Array.prototype.sort() calls the comparator for identical values;
    Iterator.prototype.constructor and [Symbol.toStringTag] setters;
    Iterator.concat() return(); RegExp named group limit, 'v' class
    escapes and out of memory paths; TypedArray.prototype.with()
    conversion order, content type checks, sort size overflow,
    JS_NewTypedArray() with argc < 3; Proxy invariant checks and ownKeys
    results; ToPropertyDescriptor exceptions; JSON.stringify() with a
    rope 'space'; interruptible Array iteration methods; module identity
    keyed by import attributes, re-export errors, spurious unhandled
    rejection of throwing modules; for await return() semantics;
    multiplicative property hash; bytecode reader hardening;
    JS_DetachArrayBuffer() double free; resolving functions on out of
    memory; JS_NewCConstructor() leak; allocation size overflows;
    std: FILE leak, std.evalScript() interrupt handler, loading pipes
    and /proc files, std.open() 'x' mode, std.popen() modes
  - immutable ArrayBuffers (ArrayBuffer.prototype.transferToImmutable(),
    sliceToImmutable(), immutable; JS_SetImmutableArrayBuffer(),
    JS_IsImmutableArrayBuffer()); the buffers of 'bytes' modules are
    immutable
  - performance is part of the engine (JS_AddPerformance(), added by
    JS_NewContext()) and has performance.timeOrigin
  - C API: JS_NewCClosure(), JS_NewCFunction3(), JS_NewCFunctionData2(),
    JS_NewPrivateSymbol(), JS_Eval2(), JS_EvalThis2(), JS_ReadObject2(),
    JS_WRITE_OBJ_STRIP_SOURCE, JS_WRITE_OBJ_STRIP_DEBUG,
    JS_SetDumpFlags() and JS_GetDumpFlags() (DUMP_* options become
    runtime JS_DUMP_* flags, built with CONFIG_DUMPS=y),
    JS_AddRuntimeFinalizer(), JS_SetModuleNormalizeFunc2(),
    JS_GetGCThreshold(), js_calloc(), js_calloc_rt() and the js_calloc
    member of JSMallocFunctions (now its first member),
    JS_NewStringUTF16(), JS_ToCStringLenUTF16(), JS_ToCStringUTF16(),
    JS_FreeCStringUTF16(), JS_FreeCStringRT_UTF16(),
    JS_New{Internal,Plain,Range,Reference,Syntax,Type}Error(),
    JS_FreezeObject(), JS_SealObject(), JS_GetClassName(),
    JS_IsDataView(), JS_IsWeakMap(), JS_IsWeakSet(), JS_IsModule(),
    JS_GetPropertyValue(), JS_GetPropertyInt64(), JS_SetPropertyValue(),
    JS_SetLength(), JS_ToNumber(), JS_ToObjectString(),
    JS_NewUint8Array(), JS_NewUint8ArrayCopy(), JS_GetUint8Array(),
    JS_FreeValues(), JS_FreeAtoms() and JS_CFUNC_DEF2(),
    JS_CGETSET_DEF2(), JS_CGETSET_MAGIC_DEF2(), JS_PROP_U2D_DEF()
  - std.writeFile(), FILE.readAsArrayBuffer(), optional position and
    length in FILE.read()/write(), FILE.write() of strings; closing
    std.in/out/err throws; os.cputime()
  - built-in 'bjson' module (replaces tests/bjson.so); its read() and
    write() take the READ_OBJ_* / WRITE_OBJ_* flags
  - JS_WriteObject()/JS_ReadObject(): RegExp, Map, Set and Symbol values
    and symbol-keyed properties; a checksum after the version byte
  - std.evalScript() options compile_only, compile_module,
    eval_function and eval_module
  - js_std_loop_once(), js_std_poll_io(),
    js_std_set_worker_new_runtime_func(), js_module_load()
  - qjs: gc(), navigator.userAgent, argv0, execArgv, -v/--version,
    -D/--dump-flags, --option=value; a file using top-level await runs
    as a module without -m
  - fixes: template literal substitutions are converted to strings in
    evaluation order; source positions of import() calls; Date.parse()
    accepts U+202F; Array.isArray() on deep Proxy chains; column of
    decorator syntax errors
- snapshot format version 8
- fixed an atom leak when reading truncated bytecode
- qjsc -fno-unused: omits the built-ins the compiled code does not
  reference (added JS_EnumCodeNames()); the qjsc executables are linked
  with the unused functions removed (the library is compiled with
  -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections), so the -fno-x options make them
  smaller without LTO; they now have DOMException, atob(), btoa() and
  performance like qjs (-fno-domexception, -fno-atob, -fno-performance)
- fixed bellard/quickjs issues:
  - an exception from the promise 'constructor' getter is thrown at the
    'await' instead of rejecting the async function (#563)
  - out of memory while creating a lazy property (JSON.parse,
    prototype, ...) no longer leaves it undefined or leaks it, and no
    longer increments the array length without adding the element
    (#580, #576)
  - WeakMap and WeakSet entries whose value references their key are
    collected in one GC (#581)
  - wrong Math.sumPrecise() result after more than 127 large values,
    and an overflow check in push_scope() (#546)
  - Number to string gives the shortest round trip string for the
    powers of two (#449)
  - use after free when a Worker is collected while its message is
    handled (#527); os.Worker throws a TypeError if no worker context
    function is set (#538)
  - Cygwin build (#575)
  - crashes when compiling under memory pressure (#528, #530, #531,
    #532): a DynBuf stops appending after an allocation error, a
    function whose bytecode could not be emitted is not compiled, and
    the parser and the variable and label resolution no longer ignore
    allocation failures
  - long BigInt operations (multiplication, division, power, string
    conversions) charge the interrupt counter and can be interrupted,
    and the regexp steps use the context interrupt counter (#546)
  - a growable SharedArrayBuffer shares its byte length between the
    threads using it and can be posted to a Worker; without a
    SharedArrayBuffer allocator, maxByteLength bytes are allocated
    (#546)
  - the runtime, context and std/os/bjson initialization report out of
    memory errors instead of crashing or asserting (#404)
  - added JS_TriggerInterruptHandler() (#387)
  - qjsc: the C modules (-M, std, os, bjson) can be imported with
    import() (#423)
  - the REPL prompt is "qjs> " (#564)
- qjsc: the JSON, text and bytes modules imported with attributes are
  found in the executable instead of being loaded at run time (added
  JS_SetModuleAttributes(); js_std_eval_binary_json_module() takes the
  module type)
- fixed a double free in JSON.parse() with a reviver when out of memory
- Temporal and Intl load the time zones missing from the embedded data
  from the system zoneinfo, so the default time zone is no longer
  treated as UTC on such hosts; unknown time zone names are rejected
- faster embedding API (used by rquickjs): JS_DupContext() and
  JS_FreeContext() are inline; added JS_GetFastArray(),
  JS_GetStdArrayPrototypeFlag(), JS_GetStringData(),
  JS_NewStringLatin1Len(), JS_GetTypedArrayData(), JS_FindAtomLen(),
  JS_GetPropertyStrLen(), JS_HasPropertyStrLen(), JS_SetPropertyStrLen(),
  JS_GetOwnPropertyCount(), JS_AtomGetStringData(),
  JS_NewObjectSetIsDefine(), JS_NewErrorLen(), JS_ThrowErrorLen() and
  JS_ExecutePendingJobs(); JSErrorEnum is public; JS_NewObjectFrom()
  creates the object with its final shape (cached per context);
  JS_GetPropertyStr() no longer creates an atom for an absent name
- faster errors: the default stack trace is formatted on first read,
  error objects reuse a cached shape and the messages are built without
  printf (throw + catch about 4x faster); the JS_Throw*Error() messages
  are no longer cut at 255 bytes
- faster strings: UTF-8 decoding and the atom lookup of UTF-8 keys scan
  several bytes at a time, String.prototype.repeat() of one character
  uses memset
- JS_GetTypedArrayBuffer() returns the current length of length-tracking
  views

